WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.930
- What is the shadow docket
on the Supreme court?

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:04.320
Well, effectively there are

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.410
two different dockets or lists of

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.980
cases before the Supreme court.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.380
There are the merits cases
on the merits docket,

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.100
where the court will
entertain extensive briefing.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.310
The parties will come in

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.940
and have oral argument before the court,

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.070
and then they will issue a long opinion

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.310
agreeing with one party

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.550
and disagreeing with another party.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.790
That's the normal
process, the merit stock.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.210
And then there is the shadow docket,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.410
which is largely made up of
cases that are asking for

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.430
emergency relief from the court.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.230
They're saying that they can't
wait for a mayor's decision.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.840
So they ask for an emergency
temporary restraining order

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.480
or an injunction from the Supreme court

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.320
often in these kinds of cases,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.290
that emergency relief
is the whole ball game.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.880
So if you're dismissing this thing

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.950
and not granting the emergency relief,

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.730
then there's no point in going forward

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.090
on a merit's decision.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.580
As of the last four years,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.590
the Supreme court has been

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.810
using the shadow docket to

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.240
dispose of cases without having

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.530
any precedential effect and

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.410
often with no opinion whatsoever,

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.140
no explanation of why they
held the way that they held.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.743
And that's probably not good for anyone.

